# A prompt chunk's sparse attention, faster at a rank's heads (both on the 2,048 selected tokens of every sparse row):
#
# - latent.sparse_onepass at up to 16 heads a rank (four Sparks): its one 16-row tile on 4 warps instead of 8, the same
#   bits (measured on GB10, FP8 and bf16 caches, 1 to 16 heads); 6.6 -> 4.8 ms a 2,048-row chunk-layer at 32k tokens,
#   7.9 -> 5.7 ms at 128k (FP8). More heads keep 8 warps and one 32-row tile (two 16-head programs a row read every key
#   twice: slower at 128k).
# - TF_GLM_MSA=1 (off by default): msa.cu, Mia's sparse attention for Flash's prompt rows on the FP8 latent cache, in
#   place of sparse_onepass. One CUDA block a row; the rank's heads as one m16 tensor-core tile (up to 16, 4 warps) or
#   two (17-32: two and three Sparks, 8 warps); each warp owns 128 latent columns of one m tile; a tile of 16 keys is
#   loaded one tile ahead into registers and converted to bf16 once for every head of the row (FP8 code x the row's
#   power-of-two scale, exact; with two m tiles the column group's two warps each convert half the keys into a
#   double-buffered region and meet at a pair barrier); the m tile's four warps add their partial scores in warp order
#   through shared memory; a log2-domain online softmax; O += P V on each warp's columns. A row's bits depend on its
#   query, its token list and the cache only (checked on the GPU: repeated runs and any block of rows give the same
#   bits), within bf16 rounding of exact attention (the same largest error against an fp32 reference as
#   sparse_onepass), but they are other bits than sparse_onepass's, so it stays off until the needle checks run with
#   it; a bf16 cache keeps sparse_onepass. TF_GLM_MSA joins the ranks' startup comparison.
#
# Measured on one GB10 (2,048 rows, 2,048 tokens a row, FP8, ms a chunk-layer; sparse_onepass with the change above ->
# msa): 32 heads (TP=2) 9.5 -> 7.1 at 32k, 10.1 -> 9.1 at 128k; 22 heads (TP=3) 9.9 -> 6.8 and 9.9 -> 8.4; 16 heads
# (TP=4) 4.8 -> 3.1 and 5.7 -> 4.6. Flash has 11 such layers a chunk.
#
# Provenance and credit: adapted from the GLM-5.3 recipe's kernel 2 (its patch 0150, Mia's AI Lab) to Flash's latent
# (512 wide, no rotary part) and to two m tiles; that kernel takes design points from drowzeys' one-pass prompt
# attention (github.com/drowzeys/TensorFold, branch glm53-tp4-2026-10-05, e91312a) and from BertholomusAI (Albert
# Lee)'s prompt sparse attention (github.com/bertholomus/TensorFold, branch glm-dsa-tp4, 8f649f1). No code was copied
# from either.
